| Buying wishes would make the game too easy.
| Remember that with a pick-axe it is easy to steal something valuable
| and sell it back again, and again, and again....
| So you would effectively have an infinite amount of wishes, and after
| wisiting such a shop you could win the game with no problems at all.
| The shop keepers should be more intelligent, so that if you try
| to sell something stolen to them, they would identify the item as stolen
| and call the kops.  They should also get mad if I dig through their
| walls, demand payment and repair it quickly.

I disagree - Wishs should be able to be bought at an extermly high price
however it should not be offered if the person stole things or destroied
shops (just about everyone). IE: it can be a different `style' to play
without robbing shops and the sale of wishes compensant. Of course
only shops on levels greater than, say, 15, should sell wishs.

The  robing items, sell items for money, purcase WISH, and loop
would not and should not be allowed.

 The WISH item is only a suggestion and if it unbalances the game should
not be allowed.  The above list is just a simple idea to enhance the value
of shop keepers to the game, stop people killing them for thier money,
prevent shop robbery (maybe to allow lawfuls to be realy properly lawful),
and to provide an outlet for money.

The Map level item could also map levels other than the one the shop is on?
though a `Map Other Level' could and I think should be more expensive.

Suggestion (to this News Group) Welcome.


